  "notes": {
    "promise-keeper": "Turns answers drawn at random into answers that keep a dependency's promises, and decides what survives a restart.",
    "promise-keeper.calcs.fresh": "The fresh answer: the value drawn, if it is not one of the values answered before (the same number, or the same text). Otherwise, if it is a number, one more than the largest number answered before; if it is a text, the text drawn followed by \"#\" and the number of values answered before (counting every value given, of either kind).",
    "promise-keeper.calcs.increasing": "The answer of a query that promises never to answer less than before. If it has not answered before (`previous` is null), the value drawn. Otherwise the previous answer plus the increment `delta`, but not more than `max` when a maximum is given.",
    "promise-keeper.calcs.restart": "The system restarts. A component that is durable keeps its state and data; any other starts again.",
    "promise-keeper.does.beginFreshNumber": "The fresh answer of a query that answers numbers is decided next, for the number drawn. No value answered before has been given yet.",
    "promise-keeper.does.beginFreshText": "The fresh answer of a query that answers texts is decided next, for the text drawn. No value answered before has been given yet.",
    "promise-keeper.does.usedNumber": "A number the query answered before.",
    "promise-keeper.does.usedText": "A text the query answered before."
  },
